        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. India’s “Cockroach Janta Party” goes viral as Gen Z movement grows Asia / Pacific Issued on: 25/05/2026 - 12:31 A viral online joke in India, the “Cockroach Janta Party,” created as a parody of comments by a Supreme Court judge, has grown into a Gen Z–driven political movement with millions of followers. It promotes youth frustration with traditional politics but has also faced attempts by authorities to restrict its spread and reports of threats against its founder. Philippines: Deadly building collapse traps workers in Manila 25/05/2026 Asia / Pacific Train bombing in Pakistan: At least 24 killed, several in critical condition 24/05/2026 Asia / Pacific Coal mine explosion in China kills 90 people, state media say 23/05/2026 Asia / Pacific Deadliest coal mine explosion in China in years kills 90 people, state media say 23/05/2026 Asia / Pacific Experts urge authorities to limit number of climbers on Mount Everest 23/05/2026 Asia / Pacific Bangladesh: \"Donald Trump\" albino buffalo becomes social media star 21/05/2026 Asia / Pacific Beijing as centre stage: Trump & Putin mark 'series of diplomatic visits to the court of Xi Jinping' 20/05/2026 Asia / Pacific Xi and Putin - Leaders praise 'unshakable foundations' at Beijing talks 20/05/2026 Asia / Pacific Adani, Trump and Modi: Why US settled fraud case with Asia's richest man 20/05/2026 Asia / Pacific"
